<title>SOUTH KOREA: BOK offers to sell dlrs in forward trade - dealers.</title>
<headline>BOK offers to sell dlrs in forward trade - dealers.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The central Bank of Korea (BOK) was seen offering to sell dollars in three-month forward trading at 893.00 won during Friday's morning session to slow the U.S. unit's climb against the domestic currency, dealers said.  </p>
<p>The central bank has refused to comment on talk of its intervention in the interbank market.</p>
<p>Shortly after the offer, the won rose to 878.90 against the dollar on the spot market, against the openning at 879.00.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5644</p>
</text>
